helper `resp.Body.Close()` calls. Check the error return of the non-search request instead of ignoring it, so `resp` is never nil.\n\n### Test plan\n- Command: `go test -count=500 -race ./internal/github -run TestRetryTransportSearchSpacing`. Also run it under load, for example 4 parallel copies of that command, and run `go test ./...`.\n- Case burst-limit (`transport_test.go`): 5 searches pass, the sixth with a 1s deadline errors immediately.\n- Case spacing: the sixth search completes at least about 95ms after `start`.\n- Case non-search: `/repos/o/r` succeeds with the search limiter exhausted.\n- Mutation check in a scratch run only, reverted afterwards: change burst 5 to 4 or 6, change the interval to 10ms, or make the transport skip `t.search.Wait`. Each must fail at least one check.\n\n### Risk\nLow. Test-only change in one file, no public interface, protected path, migration or security-sensitive code touched. The remaining wall-clock dependence is the lower bound on elapsed time, which cannot fail on a slow node.\n\n### Size\nS. Files touched: `internal/github/transport_test.go`.\nEOF\ncat > .ard/410/triage-engineer.md <<'EOF'\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nRewrites the flaky search-spacing test so it no longer measures from the wrong instant. The burst and non-search checks use a long-interval limiter and a short context deadline, and the spacing check asserts only a lower bound from the start. Size S, risk low; no production code changes.\n\n## Open issues\nNone.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2404,"cache_read_input_tokens":12432,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2404},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"ses